<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">

<!--
Alabama Appellate Courts - Case Parties API Response
=====================================================

This XSD documents the JSON API response structure from the Alabama
appellate courts case parties endpoint.

API Endpoint:
https://publicportal-api.alappeals.gov/courts/{court-guid}/cms/cases/{case-uuid}/parties

URL Parameters:
- court-guid: Court GUID (e.g., "68f021c4-6a44-4735-9a76-5360b2e8af13")
- case-uuid: Case instance UUID

Query Parameters:
- sort: Sort order (e.g., "orderBy,asc&sort=partyNumber,asc")
- size: Number of results per page (typically 100)

Response Format: JSON

The response contains a list of parties involved in the case, including
their roles, attorneys, and representation status.

Example Response Structure:
{
    "_embedded": {
        "results": [
            {
                "casePartyUUID": "abc123...",
                "partyType": "Party",
                "partySubType": "Appellant",
                "partyStatus": "Active",
                "proSeFlag": false,
                "actor": {
                    "displayName": "John Doe",
                    "sortName": "Doe, John"
                },
                "legalRepresentations": [
                    {
                        "legalRepresentationUUID": "def456...",
                        "primaryFlag": true,
                        "actor": {
                            "displayName": "Jane Attorney, Esq.",
                            "sortName": "Attorney, Jane"
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "orderBy": 1,
                "partyNumber": 1
            }
        ]
    },
    "page": {
        "size": 100,
        "totalElements": 5,
        "totalPages": 1,
        "number": 0
    }
}

Party Fields:
- casePartyUUID: Unique identifier for this party relationship
- partyType: Type of party (e.g., "Party", "Attorney")
- partySubType: Specific role (e.g., "Appellant", "Appellee", "Respondent")
- partyStatus: Status of the party (e.g., "Active", "Dismissed")
- proSeFlag: Boolean indicating if party is representing themselves
- actor.displayName: Name of the party
- actor.sortName: Sortable name format (Last, First)
- orderBy: Display order
- partyNumber: Party number

Legal Representations:
- legalRepresentations[]: Array of attorneys representing this party
  - primaryFlag: Boolean indicating if this is the primary attorney
  - actor.displayName: Attorney's name
  - actor.sortName: Sortable attorney name

Common Party SubTypes:
- Appellant: Party appealing the lower court decision
- Appellee: Party defending the lower court decision
- Respondent: Responding party
- Petitioner: Party petitioning the court
- Real Party in Interest: Actual party with interest in the outcome

Data Structure Output:
Each party is converted to a dict with:
{
    "name": "John Doe",
    "type": "Party",
    "role": "Appellant",
    "status": "Active",
    "pro_se": false,
    "attorneys": [
        {
            "name": "Jane Attorney, Esq.",
            "is_primary": true
        }
    ]
}

Next Step:
After parsing parties, the scraper fetches docket entries:
https://publicportal-api.alappeals.gov/courts/{court-guid}/cms/cases/{case-uuid}/docketentries

-->

<xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
        This is a documentation-only XSD for the Alabama Case Parties API.
        The actual response is JSON, not XML.
    </xs:documentation>
</xs:annotation>

</xs:schema>
